rea inspect-vsix-package — Inspect VS Code .vsix identity, activation, contributes and ZIP contents without install or network

Usage: rea inspect-vsix-package <path> [options]

Arguments:
  path  Local VS Code .vsix package

Options:
  --max-file-bytes <value>      Maximum stable artifact bytes to read (default 64 MiB) (default: 67108864)
  --max-entries <value>         Maximum ZIP entries to inventory; exceeding the budget fails without partial success (default: 4096)
  --max-manifest-bytes <value>  Maximum expanded bytes to decode for extension.vsixmanifest and extension/package.json; exceeding the budget fails without partial success (default: 1048576)
  --max-member-bytes <value>    Maximum expanded bytes hashed for one native addon, wasm, executable, shell script, or nested archive; exceeding the budget lists the member without a digest (default: 1048576)
  --detail <complete|summary>   Deliver complete Evidence, or a summary with --evidence_output (default: complete)
  --evidence_output <string>    Save complete Evidence as a bundle; required for summary delivery. Never overwrites.

Custom Global Options:
  --timings  Write measured command timing to stderr.

